From: Code and Solder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: qca808x: diagnose first-poll phylink sequencing

For one QCA8081 first poll with copper link already established, report
software link down while leaving the physical PHY and serial link intact.
On the next real status read, normal state and link-up are reported.

This intentionally separates phylink's first down->up notification order
from late PHY copper autonegotiation and SerDes readiness. It does not
execute the real copper-link-down seed branch and is diagnostic only.

Signed-off-by: Code and Solder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c
@@ -581,6 +581,22 @@
 		}
 	}
 
+	/* Diagnostic: distinguish a false-down first PHY poll from genuine
+	 * delayed copper negotiation. Report exactly one initially-linked
+	 * QCA8081 poll as link-down, leaving the actual PHY, PCS and MAC
+	 * hardware untouched. All subsequent polls report true MDIO state.
+	 * This intentionally does not enter the genuine link-down PHY seed
+	 * configuration branch earlier in this function.
+	 */
+	if (phydev_id_compare(phydev, QCA8081_PHY_ID) &&
+	    !priv->initial_status_samples && phydev->link) {
+		phydev_info(phydev,
+			    "wave7-diag: mask-first-link copper_link=1 speed=%d reported_link=0\n",
+			    phydev->speed);
+		phydev->link = false;
+		phydev->speed = SPEED_UNKNOWN;
+		phydev->duplex = DUPLEX_UNKNOWN;
+	}
 	/* The first PHY poll can see link down and be retried one second
 	 * later. Record only already-read software status: extra MDIO reads
 	 * would perturb the very startup timing being investigated.
